=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: adding a job that is born disabled stops nothing that ran
origin: issue #181 bound — the predicate needs a runner that could run at base and cannot at head;
origin2: a placeholder e2e job switched off from birth leaves the existing suite running.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
  e2e:
    # Enable once the staging fixture lands.
    if: false
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pytest tests/e2e
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
